                  <provenance type="#e s"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_468">Roche, Yorkshire.
                        Cistercian abbey of St Mary the Virgin</orgName><p>Old flyleaves
                        gone.</p><p>'Liber sancti Marie de Rupe' (fol. 1r).</p><p>'I' 'II' 'III' in
                        the margins at intervals, as in Laud Misc. 308, 309. Thus, 'I' is opposite
                        the first line of col. 1 on fol. 1, 'II' is opposite the second line in col.
                        2 and 'III' is five lines from bottom of col. 2. The figures occur in
                        exactly the same positions in Laud Misc. 308. This is presumably a companion
                        volume to Cambridge UL Gg. 3. 33, which contains the second part of
                        Lethbertus, has similar writing and also the Roche ex libris on fol.
                     1r.</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">'Hugh Cressy', fol. 1r, i.e. Hugh Cressy (c.
                     1605--1674), formerly chaplain to Thomas, Lord Wentworth, later (1649) a
                     Benedictine at Douai.</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Given to the Bodleian by Archbishop William
                     Laud in 1639. Laud was Cressy's patron. (See further M. Carter in Notes and
                     Queries 63 (2016) 19--22.)</provenance>
               </history>
            </msDesc>
